stateDiagram-v2
    %% Durable child of OperatorSignInFlow; the parent stays SESSION_ISSUANCE_PENDING.
    state "PENDING id=10" as PENDING
    state "SESSION_SELECTED id=20" as SESSION_SELECTED
    state "RESOLVED id=100" as RESOLVED
    state "EXPIRED id=910" as EXPIRED
    state "CANCELLED id=920" as CANCELLED

    [*] --> PENDING: issue!
    PENDING --> SESSION_SELECTED: select_session!
    PENDING --> RESOLVED: explicit POST continue / finalize_for_session_issuance!
    PENDING --> EXPIRED: expiry
    PENDING --> CANCELLED: cancel!
    SESSION_SELECTED --> RESOLVED: explicit POST continue / finalize_for_session_issuance!
    SESSION_SELECTED --> EXPIRED: expiry
    SESSION_SELECTED --> CANCELLED: cancel!

    note right of PENDING
        Operator ownership and evidence binding are rechecked at every step.
        Parent flow, optional OIDC transaction, browser binding and challenge
        are checked under the realm Ticket locks.
    end note
    note left of PENDING
        R2-WU01 implemented (nine.md P-8): the open child is the
        org waiting unit (N=1, slot N+1). Under the canonical actor
        lock and OP writer, elapsed open rows become EXPIRED before
        issue! claims waiting_slot=1. A second live lease raises the
        named occupied-slot outcome; R2-WU02 maps it at the root
        admission boundary to the existing generic :session_limit_conflict
        result with HTTP 403, without changing the existing flow or lease.
        The waiting unit may only select, explicitly continue the bound flow, or cancel;
        it never reaches MFA reset or any full-access page. Selection does not revoke.
    end note
    note right of RESOLVED
        AuthenticationBase#log_in finalizes the parent and child in one OP transaction.
        If capacity is already free, selected facts are retained and no session is revoked.
        If capacity is full, the selected target is revalidated and revoked atomically.
        Terminal states release waiting_slot and are immutable.
    end note
